{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_from_linking","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_from_linking","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.not_skeinMassDecomposition_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.not_skeinMassDecomposition_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/skein_mass_from_linking.lean#L144-L155","doc":"**The decomposition is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why\nit is named rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nAt `mass = 1` with `Q = mass_Hopf = 0` and no constituents, it reads\n`1 = 0`.  Recorded as a theorem so the module docstring's argument is\nchecked rather than asserted, and so a later attempt to \"finish\" this file\nby adding a `sorry` over free data fails against a standing\ncounterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_torus_constituents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_torus_constituents","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/skein_mass_from_linking.lean#L126-L142","doc":"**Torus-knot specialisation** — *derived* from the decomposition rather\nthan projected.\n\nWhen every constituent is a torus knot (`Vol(Kᵢ) = 0` for all `i`, the\nhyperbolic volume of a torus knot vanishing), the constituent sum drops and\nthe hadron mass is pure linking energy, `𝔪(H) = Q(q) · 𝔪(L_Hopf)`.\n\nThis is the one step the manuscript's proof actually derives, and it is the\nreason the decomposition is worth naming: it is a hypothesis something is\nproved *from*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_from_linking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.skein_mass_from_linking","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/skein_mass_from_linking.lean#L113-L124","doc":"**The claim of `lem:skein-mass-from-linking`**, as a proposition over\ncaller-supplied data:\n\n`𝔪(H) = Q(q) · 𝔪(L_Hopf) + Σ_{i < n} Vol(Kᵢ) / ℏ_q²`\n\nwith `ℏ_q = hbarQ q`.  **Named, not asserted** — see the module docstring\nfor why neither a projection nor a `sorry` is the honest form here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:skein-mass-from-linking","label":"lem:skein-mass-from-linking","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/skein-mass-from-linking.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/skein_mass_from_linking.lean#L105-L111","doc":"Substrate q-Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`.\n\nA definition rather than a data field with a `hbar_q_def` hypothesis: as a\nfield an instance chooses `hbar_q` and the constraint merely records the\nchoice, whereas here the manuscript's relation holds by construction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}